{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>ופקדתי עליכם.</b> Like a man appointed over another — he does his will with him." "<b>בהלה את השחפת ואת הקדחת.</b> Known illnesses. And the meaning of <b>את</b> is 'with.'" "And the meaning of <b>בהלה</b> — that you will panic and not know what to do. And some say: כי בהלה is like 'suddenly.' And many said that השחפת and הקדחת are two diseases of seed, like השדפון and הירקון, for thus it is written later, 'and you shall sow in vain.' But there is no need, for its meaning is that illnesses will come upon them; and if enemies come against the villages, they will eat the seed, for there is no one who goes out against them to drive them away." "And the meaning of <b>מכלות עינים.</b> That these illnesses will dim the eyes and the soul will ache. And the alef is missing from the word ומדיבות נפש, and likewise from the word שקר מזין. And some say that עינים is from the word for body, because of ומדיבות נפש, but there is no need."], :book :leviticus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {3 "The phrase 'ומדיבות נפש' appears to be a citation or reference to a related biblical phrase; the alef-deficiency note may concern the word מדבר/מדיבות in a parallel verse. The precise verse allusion is uncertain."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:12:48.515800764Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}